UPSERT finding:alist_dump_stale_caps SET status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-09-05',
 title='The d3dcap shim alist_<n>.bin still carries the OLD 2026-09-03 object caps that were fixed only in the agent',
 statement='mvc-live-skins-quarters/d3dcap/dllmain.cpp dumpAObjs: for (k = 0; k < 8) and if (size < 0 || size > 0x1000 || len + 0x50 + size > 0x1400) break -- 8 records, 4 KB per record, 5 KB per object. RetroReceipts-agent agent/src/harvest.rs:466 has AOBJ_MAX_BYTES = 0x20000 and AOBJ_MAX_RECS = 128 since 0.3.41, because those exact caps were the root cause of the part-of-the-background-missing bug. The shim was never updated. Measured on the 2026-09-05 capture: the two 548-vertex and two 310-vertex spinning stage props (list 5, obj 0x120105D8 and 0x120144F8) ship a 24-byte header with ZERO records in all 300 alist files, because their FIRST record payload exceeds 0x1398 bytes and the walk breaks immediately.',
 consequence='alist_<n>.bin is NOT ground truth for object bytes. Any coverage or reconstruction measurement that sources object geometry from alist has zero geometry for exactly the large props, independently of anything the harvest does, and will report them as uncovered. d3dcap/replay/worldgeo_gate.py silently skips them (it requires the raw object bytes to be present). The node ENUMERATION in alist is still sound -- same predicate, same lists, no 96 cap.',
 fix='Raise dumpAObjs caps to match harvest.rs (0x20000 / 128) and re-capture, or source object bytes from the live process rather than alist.';
RELATE finding:alist_dump_stale_caps -> cites -> source:cap_rrcap_4219_4518 SET id='alist_caps_cap';
UPSERT finding:alist_dump_stale_caps SET status='confirmed';
